{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-tirewear-fixture",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.1's per-fixture document, at fixture scale: `process-tirewear` as a thin document mounting a shared one. It holds no data, no shape, no metaparameters and no logic — only this metadata, the enum union, and one top-level `models` entry that is a `{ref}` to `tirewear_mount.esm`, which carries the 49 `data_sources` and mounts `tirewear_logic.esm` in turn. Three documents and two mount edges, emitting the same 375 rows as the inlined `fixtures/process-tirewear.esm`, byte for byte.\n\nWHY IT COULD NOT EXIST BEFORE 2026-09-14. The loader API bound a `data_source`'s discovered `extent` only at the ROOT document, so the root had to declare every metaparameter those extents bind — here 48 names and 247 lines that configured nothing, in every fixture — even though the logic half declares the same names and owns the axes they size (finding F50). EarthSciAST PR #317 binds a discovered extent in whichever document of the assembly declares the name, at either mount form and transitively, so this document declares none.\n\nWHY THE ENUMS ARE HERE. They are most of this file, and the build does not need them: the same document without them emits the same bytes. `tools/check-conventions.py`'s `assembly-enums` rule requires every assembly to carry the union of what it mounts, because enums merge first-wins across a mount and a same-name symbol at a different value is applied silently (F13). EarthSciAST PR #353, open at the time of writing, resolves a mounted file's enum ops against its own `enums` block; when it lands, re-read F13 and that rule before copying this block into a thirtieth fixture.\n\nWHAT IT DOES NOT DO YET is configure anything. It mounts the only catalogue this fixture has, the process snapshot. The document PLAN.md §7.5 step 7c′ wants reads the monolithic default database from the shared document and carries only this fixture's runspec selections here; that needs the generators upstream of tire wear ported, and is the next step rather than this one.\n\nHOW IT IS CHECKED. run-tests.sh's 7c stage emits this document's relation and compares it byte for byte with the inlined fixture's output from the same run, exactly as it does for `tirewear_mount.esm`, and asserts that this document declares no `data_sources`, `metaparameters`, `index_sets` or model of its own — so it cannot grow back into a mechanical copy without the suite saying so."
  },
  "enums": {
    "pollutant": {
      "TotalEnergyConsumption": 91,
      "PetroleumEnergyConsumption": 92,
      "FossilFuelEnergyConsumption": 93
    },
    "process": {
